 if len(files)==4:
  meta={'id':ASSET,'version':'1.0.0','category':'scenes','assetKind':'scene','theme':'textile','style':'source-preserved-low-poly','title':TITLE,'description':'One static whole textile hand-tool preparation-tray scene, one scene and zero new independent models. The entire qualified long-shaft drop spindle occupies a full-length low left channel, retaining its complete tapered shaft, thin bored whorl, contrasting rim and open terminal hook. The whole qualified lucet-style fork rests in a separate shorter higher right bay, retaining both outward horns, full through-eye and integral flattened grip. Both originals preserve every complete GLB buffer, normal, material dictionary, face assignment and internal hierarchy at unit scale under translations only. One newly authored continuous open-front tray is the only scene environment: two full parallel side bays have unequal floor heights, a complete longitudinal central divider, both outer rims and a continuous back rim. The full original rim facet of the spindle and the entire flat underside of the lucet have measured contact on their respective floors; neither tool supports or intersects the other. Unlike the rear-high broad gilding cushion seat and lower front burnisher ledge, this is a longitudinal divided tool organizer; unlike the three-bay sewing tray with two rear pockets and front cross-channel, this has two lengthwise bays and genuinely stepped floors. No tool part extracted, scaled, recoloured or recounted. No connecting yarn, fibre, unfinished cord, cloth, person or working procedure is supplied. Static category-level handcraft exhibit only, not tool compatibility, spinning or cord-making instruction, thread production, hand access, capacity, load, balance, stability, manufacture or safety capability. No rigging, animation or interaction.','bounds':dict(zip(['x','y','z'],[hi[k]-lo[k]for k in range(3)]),unit='m'),'triangles':triangle_count,'materials':7,'files':files,'status':'review','license':'All rights reserved'}
  (OUT/'metadata.json').write_text(json.dumps(meta,indent=2)+'\n')
